				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				103,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Element submodule to latest\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing critical bundling fixes and initialization order corrections:\n\n1. Output: Add HoistFunctionDeclarations and RewriteStaticBlockSelfRef transforms to fix TDZ errors in bundled VS Code after Rollup concatenation converts function declarations to expressions. Also updates InjectNameShim CSP and RewriteWorkbenchBaseURL for proper module graph tracking.\n\n2. Sky: Fix workbench initialization order by removing static pre-import of desktop.main.js that was breaking Electron service registration. Dynamic import now correctly sets up _VSCode_FILE_ROOT, NLS, and configuration before desktop.main.js module-initializers run.\n\n3. Cocoon: Bump protobufjs from 8.0.1 to 8.0.3.\n\nImpact: Bundled workbench now boots correctly under Tauri/WKWebView with proper initialization order and TDZ-safe transformed code.",
			"SHA": "94e6e9f950c8e4fa8276c736d41f0d8cfdea1ca8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T05:27:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				103,
				13
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Land): Standardize environment variable naming to single-word PascalCase verbs\n\nMajor refactoring across all Land configuration files adopting a consistent naming convention. Every Land-introduced env var is now a single-word, action-oriented, present-tense verb with no LAND_ prefix or multi-word concatenation:\n\n• Tracing: LAND_DEV_LOG → Trace\n• Rendering: LAND_ENABLE_WIND → Render\n• Extension handling: LAND_SKIP_BUILTIN_EXTENSIONS → Skip, LAND_AUTO_INSTALL_EXTENSION_DEPS → Install\n• Process spawning: LAND_SPAWN_COCOON → Spawn\n• Bundling: BUNDLED_WORKBENCHES → Pack, LAND_BUNDLED_BOOT → Boot\n• Node resolution: LAND_NODE_BINARY → Pick, LAND_NODE_MIN_MAJOR → Require\n• PostHog telemetry: Complete overhaul to {Authorize,Beam,Report,Throttle,Buffer,Batch,Cap,Replay,Ask,Brand}\n\nChanges span .env.Land.*.Sample files, all build scripts (Maintain/Debug, Maintain/Release, Maintain/Integration), PostHogCapture, TierEnvironment, turbo.json globalEnv, and Cargo.toml's new [patch.crates-io] section for Tauri ecosystem vendoring.\n\nImpact: Consistent developer experience across all Land build profiles; future tooling can rely on predictable, discoverable environment variable names.",
			"SHA": "a2cb235ef0d4830020fd943ee71d0accd910f370"
		},
